.TH RGBEAST 1 "November 2026" "rgbeast 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rgbeast \- RGB lighting control for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbeast
.RB [ \-\-session ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B RGBeast
shows every lighting device the
.BR rgbeastd (8)
daemon found and lets you set colours, effects, brightness and speed, light
everything the same colour, and save scenes. The app never touches hardware:
all changes go through the daemon's D-Bus API and are authorised by polkit.
Launching it again brings the open window to the front.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-session
Talk to a daemon on the session bus instead of the system bus (development against
.BR "rgbeastd \-\-session \-\-simulate" ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
.B rgbeast \-\-help
also lists development options for screenshots and self-tests.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RGBEAST_BUS=session
Talk to a daemon on the session bus (development against
.B rgbeastd \-\-session \-\-simulate
).
.TP
.B QT_SCALE_FACTOR
Scale the window, as for any Qt application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rgbeast/scenes.json
Saved scenes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rgbeast/settings.json
Window size, last device and whether the preview animates.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rgbeastd (8)
